iOS keyboard layout change: UIKit's input-mode notification reaches GPUI's on_keyboard_layout_change.

What: gpui_ios's `Platform::on_keyboard_layout_change` dropped its callback (the gap audit's "layout change a
no-op"), so `App::on_keyboard_layout_change` observers never ran on iOS. It now observes
`UITextInputCurrentInputModeDidChangeNotification` (the user switching layout or language with the globe key, a
hardware keyboard's shortcut, or the emoji keyboard) and runs the callback on the foreground executor, after UIKit's
callback unwinds, as gpui_ios already does for display notifications (the notification can arrive inside a UIKit
text-input call, while GPUI's app may be borrowed). A second registration replaces the first; the observer is
removed on drop with the display observers. `keyboard_layout()` still names one layout: GPUI rereads it and its
mapper on each change, as on macOS.

Why: GPUI rebuilds keymap state and notifies apps on a layout change; on iOS that never happened. The platform's
observers are private to gpui_ios, so neither a Parallax crate nor an extension trait can add it. cfg: the crate's
own (iOS). Written after gpui_macos's `on_keyboard_layout_change` (an input-source notification calling the stored
callback) and gpui_ios's own display observers; no Flutter counterpart (Flutter has no layout-change event).

Upstream PR: not filed yet.

